ue, error rate 0.002. v2.3.1 remains unhealthy in production and needs investigation before any redeploy. v2.3.1-rc was unhealthy in staging and was not involved in the rollback."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, and it may or may not have been created. I'll check the incident list before retrying so I don't open a duplicate page.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01LNfF8SkmnSAkSVJz9sinc4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again (error rate 0.002, down from 0.18).\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 is unhealthy there, and v2.3.1-rc was only ever deployed to staging. The first rollback attempt failed partway through, after us-east, leaving the service mixed across versions. I retried and it completed in all regions.\n- **Incident:** The first attempt to open the SEV2 incident timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying, and INC-0001 was already open with the SEV2 severity and a full summary of the rollback. I did not create a duplicate.\n\nv2.3.1 is still unhealthy in production and should be investigated before anyone redeploys it. I did not need change-manager approval, since v2.3.0 has a healthy production history.", "type": "text"}]}]}